## Status

Fixed on 2026-10-24. The frontmatter selector used the class `front-matter`; Muya's block is `pre.mu-frontmatter`, so the daily-note editor now hides that and the 2 pt rule targets it too. The math rule had set `vertical-align: baseline` on the inline-block wrapper, whose baseline comes from the zero-size source span; the wrapper now flows inline so KaTeX provides the baseline. Checked by reading Muya's inline-math renderer and CSS; not seen on screen here, since this machine has no display.


## bug in explorer at startup

