### Status

Fixed on 2026-10-24. `vue-pdf-embed` carries its own copy of pdf.js and points the worker at `./pdf.worker.mjs`, a path relative to the page that exists neither in the dev server nor in the built app, so every load failed. The pane now renders pages on canvases with `pdfjs-dist` directly, whose worker URL Vite emits as an asset (the search indexer already used it); the dependency is removed. The error text, when any, is shown in full. PDFs and drawings opened from the explorer, from links or after generating a report fill the editor column in a viewer overlay with a close button and Escape; "Open in split" still gives a pane.

## back to file explorer

I open the app and I can see the file explorer.
I open either the search or the events interfaces and I can see them fine.
I close search or events and I get back to "No Data", no file explorer.

### Status

Fixed on 2026-10-24. In lazy mode `el-tree` fills its root level from the `load` callback when it is created and from the `data` prop only on later changes. The explorer returned an empty root level from `load`, so a remount with the roots already known showed "No data". The roots are now served from both paths.

## closing the PDF view

I can now see a PDF but then the upper controls
to close the view or increase or decrease the size are visible but nresponsive
so I cannot close the pdf view

### Status

Fixed on 2026-10-24. The viewer overlay began at the top of the editor column, under the fixed title bar, whose window-drag region takes the clicks of anything drawn beneath it. The viewer and kanban overlays now start below the title bar, and pane headers are marked as no-drag regions.

## lazygit unresponsive

I can see the lazygit interface when i click on the icon
but it is unresponsive
no key works except esc to close it

### Status

Fixed on 2026-10-24. xterm.js does not take keyboard focus after `open()`, so keystrokes kept going to the editor; Escape reached the overlay's own handler for the same reason. The terminal now takes focus when it opens, when lazygit starts, and on any click in the pane.

# 23 feat: frontmatter blocks collapsible

when a md doc open, the block is collapsed,
a greyed "metadata" with a + icon,
on click it opens,
editable, with a - icon on rightr top to collapse

## Design

Done on 2026-10-24. `cazalla/renderer/editor/frontmatterFold.ts` is attached to every registered Muya instance (primary editor and file panes). It watches the editor DOM for `pre.mu-frontmatter`. A block seen for the first time, that is a freshly opened document, gets the class `cz-fm-collapsed`: the block shrinks to one line showing a greyed "+ metadata" label and its content is hidden but still present for Muya. Clicking the block expands it and places the cursor as usual; a +/− button floats over the block's top-right corner, positioned from outside Muya's DOM so the engine's re-rendering is not disturbed, and collapses or expands it. Moving the cursor into a collapsed block with the keyboard expands it, so hidden text is never edited. The daily-notes pane keeps hiding its frontmatter entirely.

# 24 colors in the file explorer

right noe the only color is green for open.
that's out.
I want red for the folders corresponding to projects,
and for files, green if git changed, blue if git untracked
parent dirs inherit blue green or mix
on inheriting project folder mixes red with blue or green or both

or something like that,
mark project folders with color
and visualize git status witrh color.

## Design

Done on 2026-10-24. The green for open files is gone. Project folders (paths listed in `_metadata/projects`) show a red folder icon. Names are coloured by git state: green for files git reports as changed (modified, added, renamed, deleted), blue for untracked; a folder takes the state of its descendants, teal when both occur below it. A project folder with changes therefore shows a red icon with a green, blue or teal name. The state comes from `git status --porcelain=v1 -z --untracked-files=all` run by the main process in the content folder (`cazalla/main/git.ts`, one registration line) and refreshed after tree events, moves and Refresh. Without git or a repository nothing is coloured.

# 25 bug the PDFs are rendered wrong

like twice reflected,
upside down and left right

## Status

Fixed on 2026-10-24. The pane set a device-pixel transform on the canvas context and also handed the canvas to pdf.js, which applies its own viewport transform; the two compounded into a 180° turn. The pixel ratio now goes into the viewport scale and pdf.js alone draws into a reset context.
